      "side": 1,
      "message": "That doesn\u0027t seem to be enough to catch the issue (unless I miss smth).\nWhen you run _cpri__AESEncryptCFB(out, ..., len, in) and pass len, for which len%16 !\u003d 0, it writes more than len bytes to out. So, it\u0027s necessary to allocate a separate buffer first, memset(buf, 0, len+16) before calling _cpri__AESEncryptCFB(buf, ...) and then verify that bytes past buf+len remained zeroes, before copying buf to cmd_body, and report error if that\u0027s not the case.\n\nSame for other modes.",
